  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 0.6.3, package.json says 0.1.0.",
        "  The App Store and the server read info.xml; everything on the node side reads package.json. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying two version numbers, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "webclient/ is read at run time and is not in the shipped file set: lib/Controller/WebClientController.php:120 reaches it through __DIR__.",
        "  A release ships only the paths of the keep set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk), so the tarball lacks it and the app fails in the code that reads it, while the build and the packing pass. In ncmake.mk, keep_extra += webclient ships it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is flowline, the checkout directory is nextcloud-flowline.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
        "PHP floor stated once: composer.json requires php ^8.2; appinfo/info.xml declares no php dependency.",
        "  Nothing contradicts anything here. Stating it in both places is what keeps a composer install from resolving packages for a PHP the server will not run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (.eslintrc.cjs, superseded form), Stylelint (stylelint.config.cjs), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (tests/phpunit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php).",
        " ESLint is configured in .eslintrc.cjs: ESLint 9 reads the flat config only; the eslintrc form, an .eslintrc file or the eslintConfig key in package.json, is ignored unless the run is pinned to ESLint 8.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence AGPL-3.0-or-later (appinfo/info.xml, package.json, composer.json).",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml links its repository and its bug tracker."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 33 to 36; the oldest maintained major is 32 (as of 2026-09), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node 24 stated in .nvmrc, within package.json engines.node ^24.0.0.",
        "  The workflows read node-version from a variable, which is not resolved here, so whether CI builds on that major is not decidable from the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "lockfiles",
      "lines": [
        "package-lock.json (lockfileVersion 3) and composer.lock in the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "ncmake-bootstrap",
